// Zed debug configuration for WHPH (Flutter).
// The Flutter project lives in `src/`, so cwd points there.
//
// `useFvm` is REQUIRED: the Dart extension does not auto-detect FVM. Without it
// the adapter looks for a bare `flutter` on PATH and aborts with
// "flutter not found in PATH" — this project pins Flutter via FVM (src/.fvmrc)
// and never puts a plain `flutter` on PATH.
//
// NIXOS NOTE: the extension resolves the binary with worktree.which("fvm")
// BEFORE this config's `env` map is applied, and it ignores `customTool`
// entirely (zed-extensions/dart, src/dart.rs). A project-local PATH override
// therefore cannot make it enter the Nix dev shell, and the Linux build fails
// to link ("ld: cannot find -lgstapp-1.0"). The fix lives outside the repo: a
// `fvm` shim on ~/.local/bin that re-enters `nix develop` for flake projects.
// See docs/build/LINUX-DEPENDENCIES.md.
//
// `deviceId` pins the target device because multiple devices (Linux desktop +
// Chrome) are usually connected and Flutter otherwise aborts with "More than
// one device connected".
// The Dart extension requires the `type` field ("flutter" here).
// See: https://zed.dev/docs/debugger
[
  {
    "label": "whph",
    "adapter": "Dart",
    "type": "flutter",
    "request": "launch",
    "program": "lib/main.dart",
    "cwd": "$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/src",
    "deviceId": "linux",
    "useFvm": true
  }
]
